WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.800 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-The last "SNL,"

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
the last live "SNL,"
was the Eddie Murphy show.

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:04.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Whoa.
-Which was fantastic.

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:07.173
What a joy to watch.
Was it an exciting week for you?

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:10.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was freaked the hell out,
because he's just, like,

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:13.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
such a pillar of
"Saturday Night Live" history.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was --
I was so jacked up.

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:18.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You had a sketch
that was cut for time

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:21.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
they put online,
called "Aidy Bizzo."

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:23.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Where it was you and Lizzo.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:23.923 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yep.

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:26.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you, yeah.

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:29.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you -- Was that --
Was that a fun thing to do

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:31.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God.
It was a dream come true.

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:35.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, Lizzo came and was lik
spanking me at points.

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:35.769 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:37.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we were gonna wear
different outfits,

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:39.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she was like,
"No, I want to match."

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:41.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Thank you, Lizzo."

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:42.876 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:43.777 line:92%
No, it was a dream come true

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:46.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we shot with Eddie,
which was so cool.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:47.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, there was a scene
with Eddie

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:48.481 line:92%
back in the wardrobe department.

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:52.919
-Yeah, and I will say, like,
I thought we would sort of

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:54.487 line:92%
shoot anything where he wasn't

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:55.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
supposed to be there
without him,

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:57.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
but there was a point
where he was sort of, like

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:59.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
waiting to come in,
and we were just shooting.

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:01.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my line
was just to be, like,

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:05.131
"I can't believe Eddie Murphy'
hosting the show this week."

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:10.336
And feeling him, like, jus
nearby while I had to say it

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:13.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
I kept going,
"I can't believe Eddie Murra

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
is hosting the show!"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:16.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Tonight!"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:18.011 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And just pure panic.

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:19.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, of course, every time
he was like,

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:22.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
"It's Eddie Murphy!"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:25.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Yes, I know that!

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:27.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm just scared."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:29.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it happened
probably three times.

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:32.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-Which is actually too many.

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:33.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:36.329
-And it did make me scared
that my brain was broken.

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:38.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then, I will say,
he was very cool about it.

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:41.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
Later, he came by and was like
"Oh, you're so funny."

00:01:41.468 --> 00:01:44.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "That mean
a lot coming from Eddie Murray

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:46.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much."
-There you go.

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:46.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
Full circle.
-Yeah.

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:51.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You -- I want to ask,
there's a line in the song

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:52.445 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and I believe you wrote

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Aidy Bizzo song
with Michael Che.

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:56.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-"Smang" was a word

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:58.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I was not familiar with
-Yes.

00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:00.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, I would be happy
to tell you about smangin' it.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please.
-Yeah, it's basically --

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:07.727
It's sort of a combination o
to smash it or to bang it.

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:08.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
-It's to smang it.

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:11.831
-Okay, gotcha.
-And Lizzo really did tweet that

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:14.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
about Michael Che,
that she wanted to smang it.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:17.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so,
Che and I wrote it together.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.339 size:88% position:44%
And as we were sitting
to write it, I was like,

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:21.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You gotta let me smang it."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:23.309
"You've got to let me talk about
smanging it."

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he sort of, like,
begrudgingly was like, "Fine."

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:28.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I feel like, by the en
of it, he got into it.

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.250 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:33.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You also had
a fantastic sketch this year

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:35.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Harry Styles,
where he played your dog.

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:38.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:41.761
I know.
-It's a very, very funny sketch.

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:45.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
Also, very sweet.
And great payoff, I feel,

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:48.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
as though, it's a good lik
minute, 90 seconds

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:50.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
before the turn happens
in the sketch --

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
very patient
piece of sketch writing.

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:53.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I love to make
them wait for it.

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:56.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. And in this case,
the waiting was the reveal

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:59.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Harry Styles
was gonna play your dog.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:01.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was he an easy sell
or a hard sell

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:02.415 line:92%
to play your dog in the sketch

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:04.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He got right on damn board.
-Yeah?

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:08.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I mean, Harry Styles..
-Yes. He seemed --

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:10.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
He seemed incredibly game
as a host,

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:13.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
which made for a great episode
-He was so game, and, like

00:03:13.193 --> 00:03:15.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
right away, when he got to set
we were like,

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:16.729 line:92%
"You need to get on all fours,

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:19.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm gonna dangle
this garbage in your mouth

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:21.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And he was, like, totally down

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:22.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, like,
truly, the next scene,

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:25.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
we were like, "Put your head
in the garbage can,

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:27.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
pretend to be a dog
smelling garbage,

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:30.944
and put it in your mouth,"
and he was like, "Okay!"

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:31.811 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:32.779 line:92%
He is really, really great

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:35.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's all you can ask fo
from an "SNL" host.

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:37.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now Adam Driver,
which I see --

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
third or fourth time --
he's an old hand at it now

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:41.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he must be great
to work with.

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:42.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's a pro!
-Yeah.

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:44.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's gonna be so fun.
-That's awesome.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He goes hard.
And he's a true actor.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:48.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He is really a true actor
-Yeah.

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:49.095 line:92%
-And it's really fun to watch --

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:50.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not that you're
not all true actors,

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:52.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it is really fun when --
-Oh!

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:54.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think
you're a true actor?

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that would be
the funny thing about --

00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:59.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when you realize, like
there was times

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:01.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
where a host would show up
and you realize,

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:03.009 line:92%
"Oh, they only know one way.

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:05.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
They don't have like,
"I have a Broadway style,

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:07.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I have
a sketch comedy style,"

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
They only know one thing.
-Totally.

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:10.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or, like,
I've had multiple times --

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:12.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, once,
I was playing a chicken

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:15.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
who was in love
with Ryan Gosling.

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:17.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, like, at multiple points,
he was like,

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:20.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
"He really loves her,
and he wants to be with her.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:21.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-"But he can't,

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:23.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
because she's a chicken,
and he's on the run."

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:26.532
And I was like, "Oh, you're,
like, thinking about this.

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:27.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.369 line:92%
-And I, like, literally --

00:04:29.369 --> 00:04:32.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, to me, it was just like,
"Bawk bawk bawk!"

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:33.606 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:35.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"I've never thought twice

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:38.177
about a single thing I've done."
-Oh. Well, people --

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:39.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
There would be times
where someone say, like,

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:42.448
"Hey, the host has some
questions about this character,"

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:43.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'd be like,
"Oh, all I know is

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:45.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
where they stand
and what they say."

00:04:45.485 --> 00:04:46.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yes.

00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:48.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like, I put no thought
into their past,

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:50.590 size:81% position:41%
and I have no thoughts
about their future."

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:51.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Past?
-Yeah.

00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:53.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like, "What was this gu
doing last week?"

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:55.194 line:92%
I'm like, "I don't bleep] know

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:57.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was a different host
last week.

00:04:57.096 --> 00:04:58.798 line:92%
-It definitely, like, reveal

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:00.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
how absolutely
simple-minded I am,

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause I'm like,
"You want me to stand where?

00:05:02.769 --> 00:05:04.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
Be loud?
You got it."

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:05.571 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:07.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Boom!
Cash the check!

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.042 line:92%
-And, hey, it's working out.

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:11.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's working out.
Eight seasons!

00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:13.346 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:15.381 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Aidy Bryant, everyone!

